hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2999","Narrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (RA), who said:\n\The people were commanded that their last act should be (performing Tawaf) of the House.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"3000","Narrated to us by Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la, who informed us that Sufyan narrated from Sulayman al-Ahwal, who narrated from Tawus, who narrated from Ibn Abbas (RA): The people would depart in every direction. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let none of you depart until his last covenant is with the House (the Ka'bah).\"""""
